  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.1 - IMPORTANT: fixes a defect in every previous release where a fresh NuGet install rendered a bare heading instead of the forum. The installer looked for its Razor views only under the site content root, while the package deploys them next to the application binaries, so it installed placeholder templates. It now looks in both places, Razor can resolve the shipped views and partials, and the community layout no longer trips Umbraco's master-template detection. Also in this release, following a pre-release audit: Moderation actions are now ignored when the report has already been resolved, so a stale queue page cannot republish a post that was removed afterwards. A rejected edit can no longer retag a thread. Banned and muted members can no longer send direct messages. Password reset and email verification links are no longer built from an unvalidated Host header: set Community:Auth:BaseUrl (or a real AllowedHosts allow-list) on production or those emails are not sent. Account deletion now erases the member from every installed package in the suite, including page comments. Members-only board titles are kept out of public listings even when the Forum node is not at the content root, and the installer now adopts an existing Forum instead of creating a second one. Documentation and marketplace metadata corrected throughout. See CHANGELOG.md.",
  "title": "Community Forum for Umbraco",
